  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nAn upper-level low pressure system will weaken as it moves onshore \nSunday and Monday, sending embedded shortwave troughs through the \narea. The greatest precipitation chances will be limited to the \nhigher terrain. The west-central ID mountains will see a 40-60% \nchance of snow showers Sunday with lower chances Monday, with \nsimilar chances across the southwest Idaho highlands. Snow levels \nwill hover near valley floors most of Sunday through Tuesday. The \nTreasure Valley will see around a 10-20% chance of a rain/snow mix \nin the early morning hours Sunday and Monday. A brief upper-level \nridge will build in Tuesday, returning drier conditions and a slight \nwarming trend. Late Tuesday through Thursday, the overall pattern \nfavors unsettled conditions, however there is considerable \nuncertainty over the trajectory of another strong Pacific upper-\nlevel low affecting the region.",
